    {
      "id": "fs0-gw-ehJbYHJEoEGeCm",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1973.514310096795,
      "y": 1839.4469085178591,
      "width": 878.1595458984375,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 549187027,
      "version": 146,
      "versionNonce": 1505399027,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787678282065,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. JAVA STACK \nJava Stack is a memory area of the JVM used to store method execution information,\n including stack frames, local variables, method parameters, and intermediate values.\n\nWHATS STACK FRAME?\nA STACK FRAME IS THE BLCOKK OF MEMORY CREATED AFTER EACH METHOD CALLS\n \nMethod called\n     ↓\nStack Frame created\n     ↓\nStored in Java Stack\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. JAVA STACK \nJava Stack is a memory area of the JVM used to store method execution information,\n including stack frames, local variables, method parameters, and intermediate values.\n\nWHATS STACK FRAME?\nA STACK FRAME IS THE BLCOKK OF MEMORY CREATED AFTER EACH METHOD CALLS\n \nMethod called\n     ↓\nStack Frame created\n     ↓\nStored in Java Stack\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3cyUDK6-NLdnEwcoycMFb",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1940.8861063363074,
      "y": 2009.3218248404996,
      "width": 262.6203028120176,
      "height": 136.27463717262071,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
