    },
    {
      "id": "NcAscFWcZR8s5og8ToyRp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1980.4344582205235,
      "y": 2253.6262242597786,
      "width": 1470.0989990234375,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1405299933,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1971334301,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787678612336,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4.PC Register (Program Counter Register)\nDefinition\n\nThe PC Register is a small memory area in the JVM that keeps track of the address/position of the instruction currently being executed by a thread.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4.PC Register (Program Counter Register)\nDefinition\n\nThe PC Register is a small memory area in the JVM that keeps track of the address/position of the instruction currently being executed by a thread.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "sCI825XLCFoiMZs5sKJwd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1973.602614186682,
      "y": 2398.89324736941,
      "width": 1355.259033203125,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1398941427,
      "version": 74,
      "versionNonce": 1455886035,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787678845391,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5.What is the Native Method Stack?\n\nThe Native Method Stack is a JVM memory area used when a thread executes native methods.\n\nNow the obvious question is:\n\nWhat is a native method?\n\nA native method is a method whose implementation is written in a language other than Java, typically C or C++, and is accessed from Java.\n\nJava Program\n     ↓\nCalls native method\n     ↓\nNative Method Stack is used\n     ↓\nNative code executes\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5.What is the Native Method Stack?\n\nThe Native Method Stack is a JVM memory area used when a thread executes native methods.\n\nNow the obvious question is:\n\nWhat is a native method?\n\nA native method is a method whose implementation is written in a language other than Java, typically C or C++, and is accessed from Java.\n\nJava Program\n     ↓\nCalls native method\n     ↓\nNative Method Stack is used\n     ↓\nNative code executes\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
