      "seed": 1035286707,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 292226835,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787679059216,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "EXECUTION ENGINE",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "EXECUTION ENGINE",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "iPFtWFrA8yBOwYgWxA29L",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1984.3219081128668,
      "y": 3117.3234606856176,
      "width": 1105.0477294921875,
      "height": 280,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0W",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 956223677,
      "version": 71,
      "versionNonce": 856038333,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787679108675,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is the Execution Engine?\n\nThe Execution Engine is the part of the JVM that executes the Java bytecode.\n\n1.INTERPRETER \n2.JIT COMPILER\n3.GARBEGE COLLECTOR\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is the Execution Engine?\n\nThe Execution Engine is the part of the JVM that executes the Java bytecode.\n\n1.INTERPRETER \n2.JIT COMPILER\n3.GARBEGE COLLECTOR\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "X47eXsQH55H5-QDFSbfQj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1965.6342172923196,
      "y": 3445.9687323094013,
      "width": 1826.9149169921875,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1987639517,
      "version": 140,
      "versionNonce": 1844347603,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787679281931,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.INTERPRETER- The Interpreter reads bytecode and executes it instruction by instruction.\n\n\n\n2.JIT Compiler — Just-In-Time Compiler ⚙️\n\nJIT = Just-In-Time Compiler\n\nDefinition\n\nThe JIT Compiler improves performance by compiling frequently executed bytecode into native machine code during program execution.\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.INTERPRETER- The Interpreter reads bytecode and executes it instruction by instruction.\n\n\n\n2.JIT Compiler — Just-In-Time Compiler ⚙️\n\nJIT = Just-In-Time Compiler\n\nDefinition\n\nThe JIT Compiler improves performance by compiling frequently executed bytecode into native machine code during program execution.\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "l0S0DW05MY8c3dWk95fLZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1929.8162356296662,
      "y": 3899.6635363432597,
      "width": 2083.5068359375,
      "height": 245,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1672020307,
      "version": 68,
      "versionNonce": 751514333,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1787679332110,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3.Garbage Collector (GC) 🗑️\n\nThe Garbage Collector is another important part of the JVM's execution/runtime system.\n\nDefinition\n\nGarbage Collector is a JVM component that automatically identifies objects that are no longer reachable by the program and reclaims their Heap memory.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3.Garbage Collector (GC) 🗑️\n\nThe Garbage Collector is another important part of the JVM's execution/runtime system.\n\nDefinition\n\nGarbage Collector is a JVM component that automatically identifies objects that are no longer reachable by the program and reclaims their Heap memory.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
